{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f7b304173e6ed5ac","name":"F1 Exploration Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-f7b304173e6ed5ac","title":"F1 Exploration Droid","revision":21321,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:35:00Z","sha256":"fa8b60bb5796d2fcee9e94ffc9cd76040da09603173e9ece2b67b9d05a22990e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21321","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=F1%20Exploration%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f7b304173e6ed5ac","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed to be a companion and a protector for those venturing to the edge of known space and beyond, the F1 Exploration Droid packs a lot of functionality within a small frame. As a four-legged Droid, the F1 uses its low profile to its advantage as it attempts to remain hidden. Its sensor array allows the Droid to survey its environment through audio, visual, and olfactory sensors, much like a natural creature. The F1 also has a motion sensor suite to detect nearby anomalies. An ",{"tag":"a","children":["Internal Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Internal_Comlink","referenceId":"reference:7fadfdfea7aba7e9"}," enables the Droid to remain in contact when traveling far from its master's camp.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The F1's features enable the Droid to perform well as a Security Droid, even though its core programming does not emphasize that function. Although the F1 Exploration Droid's defense capabilities are not as sophisticated as other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", it can deliver a vicious bite with its mechanical jaw. However, the Droid has enough fine control over its mandible to grasp an organic creature without causing damage. This ability is particularly useful if its master is wounded; the Droid has enough strength to return its master to camp for medical attention.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["F1 Exploration Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["F1 Exploration Droid Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["5th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 16), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 15, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"http